<section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-duo"><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-circle-question"></i></span><h2>What Are Fan Sections?</h2><p>Fan sections are fan assemblies designed to become part of an HVAC or air-handling system. Their compact arrangement allows them to be incorporated into equipment where space, airflow, pressure, vibration, noise, and installation flexibility need to be considered.</p><p>The current range includes Plug Fans and Mixed Flow Fans. These configurations can be selected according to airflow requirements, static pressure, available installation space, application, and operating conditions.</p><p>Fan sections may be used in new HVAC installations as well as retrofits where an existing air handling unit needs an updated or replacement fan arrangement.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Plug Fans</h2><p>Plug fans are designed to integrate directly into ductwork or equipment. Their compact construction makes them useful for applications where available installation space is limited.</p><p>The current plug fan range covers 315 mm to 1600 mm in size, with capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH and static pressure up to 40 mmWG. The fans use an adjustable pitch impeller, providing flexibility for different airflow requirements.</p><p>Plug fans are designed to provide efficient airflow delivery with relatively quiet operation. They can be considered for HVAC systems, commercial environments, AHU applications, and equipment where direct integration is required.</p></div><div class="fcx-panel" style="grid-column:1/-1"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-fan"></i></span><h2>Mixed Flow Fans</h2><p>Mixed flow fans combine features of axial and centrifugal fans. This allows them to offer a balance between airflow and pressure for different ventilation and HVAC applications.</p><p>The current design uses a backward-curved impeller to achieve better performance and lower noise levels. Integration of the impeller with an external rotor motor is also considered during fan design.</p><p>Mixed flow fans may be used in washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public areas. Selection also considers bulk, weight, vibration, noise, durability, efficiency, and safety.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Key Features of Fan Sections</h2><p>Fan sections offer several features for modern HVAC and ventilation systems:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Plug and mixed flow fan configurations</li><li>Compact installation arrangement</li><li>Direct integration into ductwork or equipment</li><li>Plug fan sizes from 315 mm to 1600 mm</li><li>Plug fan capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH</li><li>Plug fan static pressure up to 40 mmWG</li><li>Adjustable pitch impeller for plug fans</li><li>Backward-curved impeller for mixed flow fans</li><li>Designed for efficient airflow</li><li>Lower noise design for mixed flow applications</li><li>External rotor motor integration</li><li>Suitable for AHUs and packaged HVAC equipment</li><li>Suitable for existing AHU retrofits</li><li>Suitable for industrial and commercial applications</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Technical Specifications</h2><div class="fcx-tables"><div class="fcx-tablewrap"><table class="fcx-table fcx-table--3"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Parameter</th><th scope="col">Plug Fans</th><th scope="col">Mixed Flow Fans</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Fan Type</th><td>Plug Fan</td><td>Mixed Flow Fan</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Size</th><td>315 mm to 1600 mm</td><td>Application-based</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Capacity</th><td>Up to 1,30,000 CMH</td><td>Application-based</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Static Pressure</th><td>Up to 40 mmWG</td><td>Application-based</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Impeller</th><td>Adjustable Pitch Impeller</td><td>Backward Curved</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Motor Integration</th><td>Application-based</td><td>External Rotor Motor</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Main Feature</th><td>Compact direct integration</td><td>Balanced airflow and pressure</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Noise Performance</th><td>Quiet operation</td><td>Lower noise design</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Applications</th><td>HVAC, AHUs, commercial systems</td><td>Toilets, hotels, auditoriums, airports, public areas</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div><div class="fcx-note fcx-note--wide"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-sliders"></i></span><div><p>The final fan section should be selected according to the specified airflow, static pressure, application, installation area, noise requirements, and location conditions.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>Applications of Fan Sections</h2><p><b>Fan Sections in Ahmedabad</b> are appropriate for a variety of HVAC and air-handling applications. Common applications include:</p><ul class="fcx-checks"><li>Air Handling Units</li><li>Existing AHU retrofits</li><li>Packaged HVAC equipment</li><li>Commercial HVAC systems</li><li>Industrial ventilation</li><li>Hotel ventilation</li><li>Auditorium ventilation</li><li>Airport ventilation</li><li>Supermarkets</li><li>Railway and transit stations</li><li>Public buildings</li><li>Toilet ventilation systems</li><li>Industrial air-handling systems</li></ul><p>Ahmedabad and the broader Gujarat industrial belt include GIDC estates around Vatva, Naroda, Changodar, and Sanand. These areas have textile mills, chemical and pharmaceutical plants, engineering units, and a growing automotive cluster. Many facilities run continuous processes in a hot, dry climate where reliable air movement may be important for worker comfort and process conditions.</p></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Benefits of Fan Sections</h2></div><div class="fcx-cards fcx-cards--3"><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-screwdriver-wrench"></i></span><h3>Compact Installation</h3><p>Fan sections can offer a compact airflow arrangement for HVAC equipment, making them useful where installation space is limited.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-screwdriver-wrench"></i></span><h3>Flexible Integration</h3><p>Plug fans can integrate directly into ductwork or equipment, providing flexibility for new installations as well as existing HVAC systems.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-gauge-high"></i></span><h3>Efficient Airflow</h3><p>Plug fans and mixed flow fans are designed to deliver effective airflow according to the requirements of the connected HVAC or ventilation system.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-gauge-high"></i></span><h3>Balanced Airflow and Pressure</h3><p>Mixed flow fans integrate axial and centrifugal characteristics, helping provide a balance between airflow and pressure for specific applications.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-box"></i></span><h3>AHU Retrofit Compatibility</h3><p>Ready-to-install fan sections can be used for retrofits of existing AHUs, helping upgrade or replace fan arrangements without redesigning the complete HVAC system.</p></div><div class="fcx-card"><span class="fcx-ico"><i class="fas fa-shapes"></i></span><h3>Application Flexibility</h3><p>Different fan configurations allow fan sections to be used across commercial buildings, industrial facilities, public spaces, and packaged HVAC equipment.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-blocks"><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Fan Sections Suppliers in Ahmedabad</h2><p>When selecting <b>Fan Sections Suppliers in Ahmedabad</b>, it is vital to provide complete technical information before selecting the correct configuration. Airflow, static pressure, available space, equipment dimensions, application, noise requirements, and operating conditions can all affect the selection.</p><p>For Ahmedabad projects, fan sections can be required for AHUs, AHU retrofits, packaged HVAC systems, commercial buildings, hotels, public areas, and industrial facilities. The selected fan must be properly matched with the existing or proposed HVAC system.</p></div><div class="fcx-block"><h2>Fan Sections Manufacturer in India</h2><p>For projects looking for a <b>Fan Sections Manufacturer in India</b>, technical sizing is an important part of choosing the suitable fan configuration. The equipment should be matched with the required airflow, static pressure, application, and installation conditions.</p><p>The manufacturing facility is located in Neemrana, Rajasthan. Fan sections are selected according to project requirements, with technical sizing and data available before ordering. Finished equipment can be dispatched to Ahmedabad and other places across India.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><h2>How to Choose the Right Fan Section</h2><p>Before selecting a fan section, consider the following factors:</p><ul class="fcx-checks fcx-checks--long"><li><b>Airflow Requirement:</b> Determine the specified airflow for the HVAC system.</li><li><b>Static Pressure:</b> Calculate the pressure required to overcome system resistance.</li><li><b>Fan Type:</b> Select a plug fan or mixed flow fan according to the application.</li><li><b>Available Space:</b> Check the size and installation area in the AHU or equipment.</li><li><b>Impeller:</b> Consider adjustable pitch or backward-curved impeller requirements.</li><li><b>Noise:</b> Review acoustic requirements for offices, hotels, hospitals, and public areas.</li><li><b>AHU Retrofit:</b> Check the existing equipment dimensions and connection requirements for retrofit projects.</li><li><b>Operating Conditions:</b> Consider temperature, humidity, dust, vibration, and other site conditions.</li><li><b>Maintenance:</b> Ensure enough access for inspection and servicing.</li></ul></div></section><section class="fcx-band fcx-band--alt"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-center"><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2></div><div class="fcx-faq"><details><summary>What are fan sections used for?</summary><p>Fan sections are used in HVAC and air-handling systems, such as air handling units, AHU retrofits, packaged HVAC equipment, and industrial ventilation systems.</p></details><details><summary>What types of fans are available in fan sections?</summary><p>The current range includes Plug Fans and Mixed Flow Fans.</p></details><details><summary>What is the size range of plug fans?</summary><p>The current plug fan range is available from 315 mm to 1600 mm.</p></details><details><summary>What is the capacity of plug fans?</summary><p>Plug fans are available with capacity up to 1,30,000 CMH and static pressure up to 40 mmWG.</p></details><details><summary>Where are mixed flow fans used?</summary><p>Mixed flow fans can be used in washrooms, hotels, auditoriums, stations, supermarkets, airports, and other public areas.</p></details></div><div class="fcx-center" style="margin-top:26px"><a href="product.php" class="btn-cyber btn-cyber--primary fcx-btn" title="Fan Air India Products">Learn More <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section><section class="fcx-band"><div class="fcx-wrap"><div class="fcx-cta"><h2>Conclusion</h2><p>Fan sections provide a practical and flexible solution for HVAC and air-handling systems where compact installation, efficient airflow, and application-specific fan selection are important. Plug fans offer direct integration into ductwork and equipment, while mixed flow fans offer a balance between airflow and pressure.</p><p>FanAir India Pvt. Ltd. offers fan section solutions for Ahmedabad and other places throughout India, with selection based on airflow, static pressure, application, installation area, and site conditions. Technical requirements may be reviewed before ordering to identify a suitable plug fan or mixed flow fan configuration for the project.</p><a href="../contact.php" class="fcx-cta__btn" title="Contact Fan Air India">Contact Us <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></div></div></section>
